,20912,33,73315,33,22037,1215,2383,20912,34,73315,34,42125,1215,2383,20912,35,73315,35,42125,317,24157,6405,60,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nIn isosceles triangle $ABC$, angle $BAC$ and angle $BCA$ measure 35 degrees. What is the measure of angle $CDA$? [asy]\nimport olympiad; import geometry; size(125); defaultpen(linewidth(0.8));\ndraw(circle((0,0),1));\ndot(\"$F$\",(0,0),dir(-90));\npair A = dir(160), B = dir(110), C = dir(40), D = dir(10);\ndraw(A--D--C--A--B--C);\nlabel(\"$A$\",A,W); label(\"$B$\",B,N); label(\"$C$\",C,E); label(\"$D$\",D,E);\n[/asy]","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"127b1ffef7a3bdec41382bbd4863df29f19b9f3d483fb27276d96a063b34fcc0"},"seconds":18.967915534973145,"seed":747075883868926883,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem, we need to understand the structure of the given isosceles triangle \\(ABC\\) and the relationship of point \\(D\\) with respect to the circle in which triangle \\(ABC\\) is inscribed.\n\nFirst, let's summarize the given information:\n- \\(\\triangle ABC\\) is isosceles with \\(\\angle BAC = \\angle BCA = 35^\\circ\\).\n- The measure of \\(\\angle CDA\\) needs to be found.\n\nSince \\(\\triangle ABC\\) is isosceles with \\(\\angle BAC = \\angle BCA = 35^\\circ\\), we can determine the measure of \\(\\angle ABC\\):\n\\[\n\\angle ABC = 180^\\circ - \\angle BAC - \\angle BCA = 180^\\circ - 35^\\circ - 35^\\circ = 110^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nNow, consider the cyclic quadrilateral \\(ABDC\\). Since \\(A, B, C, D\\) are points on the circle, \\(\\angle CDA\\) and \\(\\angle ABC\\) are supplementary angles (they lie on opposite sides of the cyclic quadrilateral):\n\\[\n\\angle CDA = 180^\\circ - \\angle ABC = 180^\\circ - 110^\\circ = 70^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nThus, the measure of \\(\\angle CDA\\) is \\(\\boxed{70}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{70}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true,"retains_student_answer":false},"graded_text":"To solve the problem, we need to understand the structure of the given isosceles triangle \\(ABC\\) and the relationship of point \\(D\\) with respect to the circle in which triangle \\(ABC\\) is inscribed.\n\nFirst, let's summarize the given information:\n- \\(\\triangle ABC\\) is isosceles with \\(\\angle BAC = \\angle BCA = 35^\\circ\\).\n- The measure of \\(\\angle CDA\\) needs to be found.\n\nSince \\(\\triangle ABC\\) is isosceles with \\(\\angle BAC = \\angle BCA = 35^\\circ\\), we can determine the measure of \\(\\angle ABC\\):\n\\[\n\\angle ABC = 180^\\circ - \\angle BAC - \\angle BCA = 180^\\circ - 35^\\circ - 35^\\circ = 110^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nNow, consider the cyclic quadrilateral \\(ABDC\\). Since \\(A, B, C, D\\) are points on the circle, \\(\\angle CDA\\) and \\(\\angle ABC\\) are supplementary angles (they lie on opposite sides of the cyclic quadrilateral):\n\\[\n\\angle CDA = 180^\\circ - \\angle ABC = 180^\\circ - 110^\\circ = 70^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nThus, the measure of \\(\\angle CDA\\) is \\(\\boxed{70}\\).","id":"geometry:469"}
